// REJECTS: Field 'data' is required
//
// The LEGACY `test: Single { ... }` block requires `data:` -- a bare string of test data --
// as well as `asserts:`. Both arms are optional in the grammar.
//
// Worth pinning separately from the modern testSuites form: the two blocks share the words
// `data` and `asserts` but mean different things by them (here `data` is a STRING, there it
// is a list of connection islands), and only one of the two makes `data` mandatory.
###Service
Service fixture::neg::LegacyTestWithoutData
{
   pattern: '/x';
   documentation: 'd';
   execution: Single
   {
      query: |fixture::neg::Person.all();
      mapping: fixture::neg::M;
      runtime: fixture::neg::R;
   }
   test: Single
   {
      asserts:
      [
         { [], |'x' }
      ];
   }
}
